Third-party software
--------------------
The bundled classical female bust mesh is adapted from Innerscene's CC0 1.0 graphical asset,
based on MakeHuman/MPFB CC0 assets. Concordia adds the olive crown, renderer and color treatment.
Source, exact hashes and reproducible conversion: crates/concordia/assets/concordia-model-CREDITS.md.

concordia is built from open source crates. Every release ships THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, generated by
`cargo about generate about.hbs`, containing each crate's copyright notice and license text.
Dependency licenses are enforced in CI by `cargo deny check` (see deny.toml).

Reviewed MPL-2.0 dependencies are `option-ext` (via `dirs`) and the native Mermaid parser's
`cssparser`, `cssparser-macros`, `dtoa-short` and `selectors`. These file-level copyleft libraries
are used unmodified; exact source links and license texts are included in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt.
If any are vendored or modified, those files must retain their applicable MPL notices and source
availability obligations. The exceptions are crate-specific in deny.toml.

Crossterm 0.28.1 is vendored under vendor/crossterm (MIT; see its LICENSE).
Concordia changes src/event/sys/windows/parse.rs to ignore key-release surrogate halves,
so Windows emoji input reaches the editor. Patch rationale and removal criteria: vendor/crossterm/CONCORDIA-PATCH.md.
It also exposes the shared ANSI parser to Concordia's Windows VT byte-stream input
source, preserving framed pastes. The same patch document records scope and removal criteria.
